1
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:09,100
A laptop stores 512 gigabytes.

2
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:13,420
A grain of pollen is about 25 micrometres across.

3
00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:17,140
A cruise ship weighs 100,000 tonnes.

4
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:20,700
What does micro mean: one millionth, or one million?

5
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,940
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,720
Micro means one millionth.

7
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:29,080
A micrometre is one millionth of a metre.

8
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:32,870
Remember: 1 kilometre is 1,000 metres.

9
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:37,760
1 metre is 100 centimetres, or 1,000 millimetres.

10
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:40,910
1 kilogram is 1,000 grams.

11
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,400
A prefix multiplies the unit by a power of 10.

12
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,440
Mega means a million, 10 to the power 6.

13
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:49,660
Kilo means a thousand.

14
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:51,390
Centi is one hundredth.

15
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,200
Milli is one thousandth.

16
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:57,370
Micro is one millionth, 10 to the power minus 6.

17
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:58,140
Your turn.

18
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:00,060
Giga is bigger than mega.

19
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:03,750
Is giga 10 to the power 9, or 10 to the power 6?

20
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,220
Pause the video and choose.

21
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:11,480
Giga is 10 to the power 9, a thousand million.

22
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:16,200
512 gigabytes is 512 times 10 to the 9 bytes.

23
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:19,940
Also: 1 tonne is 1,000 kilograms.

24
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:22,130
Big unit to small unit: multiply.

25
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,730
Small unit to big unit: divide.

26
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:26,190
Here is the method.

27
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:29,970
Step 1: write the prefix as a power of 10.

28
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:34,380
Step 2: convert to the base unit, like metres or grams.

29
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:37,620
Step 3: convert to the unit you want.

30
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:41,820
Step 4: check: a smaller unit means a bigger number.

31
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:44,590
A lorry carries 12.4 tonnes.

32
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:51,660
In kilograms, that is 12.4 times 1,000, which is 12,400 kilograms.

33
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:54,530
A bacterium is 3 micrometres long.

34
00:01:54,580 --> 00:02:00,880
That is 3 times 10 to the minus 6 metres, which is 0.003 millimetres.

35
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:01,620
Your turn.

36
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:03,900
A hair is 80 micrometres thick.

37
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,030
How many millimetres is that?

38
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:09,050
Pause and work it out.

39
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:12,870
1,000 micrometres make 1 millimetre.

40
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:17,670
80 divided by 1,000 is 0.08 millimetres.

41
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,120
A 6 gigabyte film is 6,000 megabytes.

42
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:26,520
And 250 microlitres of medicine is 0.25 millilitres.

43
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:29,470
Max converts 350 milligrams to grams.

44
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,610
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,730
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:37,290
Grams are bigger than milligrams, so the number must get smaller.

47
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:38,340
Divide.

48
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:43,230
350 divided by 1,000 is 0.35 grams.

49
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:49,850
The tiny parts inside computer chips are measured in nanometres, which are billionths of a metre.

50
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,860
That is why so many fit on one chip.

51
00:02:52,910 --> 00:02:54,160
One last question.

52
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:56,690
How many kilograms are in 2 tonnes?

53
00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:00,040
Pause the video and answer.

54
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:04,350
2 times 1,000 is 2,000 kilograms.

55
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:10,910
To remember: giga is 10 to the 9, mega 10 to the 6, kilo 10 to the 3.

56
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:16,460
Milli is 10 to the minus 3, and micro is 10 to the minus 6.

57
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:19,730
1 tonne is 1,000 kilograms.

58
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,420
To a bigger unit, divide.

59
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:23,870
To a smaller unit, multiply.

60
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:29,110
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.3 on Camday.
